{"name":"Cannon Ball","hex":"#484335","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cannon ball","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of cannonball."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cannon_ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cannon Ball (roller coaster)","blocks":[{"text":"Cannon Ball is a wooden roller coaster located at Lake Winnepesaukah amusement park in Rossville, Georgia, United States. The ride opened in 1967, was designed by John C. Allen, and was built by Philadelphia Toboggan Coasters. It is one of three roller coasters at the park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg/330px-The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannon_Ball_(roller_coaster)","wikidata":"Q5032751"},{"title":"Cannon","blocks":[{"text":"A cannon is a large-caliber gun classified as a type of artillery, which usually launches a projectile using explosive chemical propellant. Gunpowder was the primary propellant before the invention of smokeless powder during the late 19th century. Cannons vary in gauge, effective range, mobility, rate of fire, angle of fire and firepower; different forms of cannon combine and balance these attributes in varying degrees, depending on their intended use on the battlefield. A cannon is a type of heavy artillery weapon. The word cannon is derived from several languages, in which the original definition can usually be translated as tube, cane, or reed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg/330px-%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannon","wikidata":"Q81103"},{"title":"Round shot","blocks":[{"text":"A round shot is a solid spherical projectile without explosive charge, launched from a gun. Its diameter is slightly less than the bore of the barrel from which it is shot. A round shot fired from a large-caliber gun is also called a cannonball."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/MaryRose-round_shot.JPG/330px-MaryRose-round_shot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_shot","wikidata":"Q1723884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg/500px-The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg/1280px-The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg/500px-The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg/500px-%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg/1280px-%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x",